WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.210
Air contains oxygen.

2
00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:04.330
Water contains oxygen too.

3
00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:07.970
You can pull oxygen out of air
without any chemical reaction at

4
00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:08.810
all.

5
00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:10.990
But to get oxygen out of water,

6
00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.630
you have to make a
chemical reaction happen.

7
00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.470
Both contain oxygen, so why is
one so much harder than the

8
00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:18.230
other?

9
00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:21.050
In this mission, you'll learn
the difference between an

10
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:23.560
element, a compound and a mixture.

11
00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:27.510
You'll find out what it takes
to split a compound apart.

12
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.750
And you'll meet the physical
methods that separate mixtures,

13
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.350
like filtration, crystallisation,

14
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.810
distillation and chromatography.

15
00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:40.070
Your mission: explain why oxygen
comes out of air so much more

16
00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:42.100
easily than out of water.
